  "policy": "Every upstream DiamaneOS builds from. forks: repositories we fork and patch (the manifest overlay forks on android17 and the kernel forks pinned in config/patches.json); the fork branch is the pin and upstream is the reference it follows. sources: pinned upstream inputs that are not forked; pin names the file and field that hold the pinned value. newer: branches or tags that would supersede the followed reference, ordered by their capture group. Fairphone forks track the public-build branch where it exists, otherwise rc; CodeLinaro forks track a release tag, or the newest release branch that contains the pinned commit with its release tags as newer. Checks read remote refs only and never move a branch or push; upstream updates are rebased into a local candidate branch for build and review, and adopting one is a reviewed, signed change.",
